      <marc:subfield code="a">&quot;The classic guide for today&apos;s value investor--with the author&apos;s perspectives on the value mindset and effective stock picking Brandes on Value, by Charles Brandes examines why the value discipline to stock selection has been so successful since first introduced by Benjamin Graham in the 1930s. Includes insights into value investing in the real world; risk and risk analysis; thinking globally, active vs. passive investing; value bonds, navigating the financial crisis and Japan&apos;s lost decades; exploiting investor behavior, and insightful research from the Brandes Institute&quot;--</marc:subfield>
